.he "djformat (1)                 9/28/26                 djformat (1)"
.fo "                               -#-"
.in 5
.rm 65
.bd
NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
djformat
- format a Morrow DJ-DMA floppy diskette
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SYNTAX
.in +5
.br
.bd
djformat device [ track ]
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DESCRIPTION
.in +5
.br
Djformat runs the controller's write-track command across a diskette, one
track per ioctl, printing a line as each track is done.  It walks all 77
tracks of the 8 inch drive; the device node names the drive.  A format
blanks the diskette, so any filesystem goes with it and mkfs follows.
.sp
With a track argument, only that one track is formatted.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
EXAMPLE
.in +5
.br
.bd
djformat /dev/fla
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SEE ALSO
.in +5
.br
mkfs (1), mwformat (1)
